CUDA math policy (cuda_fast_math): fast
Metal half exp, log, exp2, log2, sin, cos and sqrt, and under cuda_fast_math=false CUDA's besides reciprocal, rsqrt and tanh, are the same kernel's f32 results rounded to half once, signed zeros, infinities and NaN included: true
Metal renders each half unary builtin as the widened f32 call narrowed once, and so does CUDA under cuda_fast_math=false: true
